## 1. Overview of the Design

| Component | Responsibility |
|-----------|-----------------|
| **KMDF Driver** (`MemRwDriver`) | - Creates a device object (`\\.\MemRw`).<br>- Exposes two IOCTLs: `IOCTL_MEM_RW_READ` and `IOCTL_MEM_RW_WRITE`.<br>- In the IOCTL callback:<br>  1. Looks up the target `EPROCESS` by PID.<br>  2. Verifies the caller has `SeDebugPrivilege` (or is running as SYSTEM).<br>  3. Calls `MmCopyVirtualMemory` to copy data between the caller’s address space and the target process.<br>  4. Returns the number of bytes transferred or an appropriate NTSTATUS. |
| **User‑Mode Client** (`MemRwClient`) | - Opens a handle to `\\.\MemRw` via `CreateFile`.<br>- Builds the input/output buffers for the chosen IOCTL.<br>- Calls `DeviceIoControl`.<br>- Prints success/failure and, for reads, dumps the data. |

Both sides use a **shared header** (`MemRwIoctl.h`) that defines the IOCTL codes and the parameter structures.

---

## 2. Shared Header – `MemRwIoctl.h`

```c
/*=====================================================================
  MemRwIoctl.h
  Shared definitions between the KMDF driver and the user‑mode client.
  =====================================================================*/

#ifndef MEMRW_IOCTL_H
#define MEMRW_IOCTL_H

#include <windows.h>
#include <winioctl.h>

#define MEMRW_DEVICE_TYPE          FILE_DEVICE_UNKNOWN
#define MEMRW_DEVICE_NAME          L"\\\\.\\MemRw"
#define MEMRW_DOS_DEVICE_NAME      L"\\DosDevices\\MemRw"

/* IOCTL codes – use METHOD_BUFFERED for simplicity */
#define IOCTL_MEM_RW_READ  \
    CTL_CODE(MEMRW_DEVICE_TYPE, 0x800, METHOD_BUFFERED, FILE_ANY_ACCESS)

#define IOCTL_MEM_RW_WRITE \
    CTL_CODE(MEMRW_DEVICE_TYPE, 0x801, METHOD_BUFFERED, FILE_ANY_ACCESS)

/*
  Parameter structure that is identical in kernel and user mode.
  The caller fills in the fields; the driver returns the number of
  bytes actually transferred in BytesTransferred.
*/
typedef struct _MEM_RW_PARAMS {
    /* [in]  ID of the target process */
    HANDLE  TargetProcessId;          // same type as ULONG_PTR (PVOID)

    /* [in]  Address in the target process to read from / write to */
    PVOID   TargetAddress;

    /* [in]  Address in the caller's process (client) buffer */
    PVOID   CallerAddress;

    /* [in]  Number of bytes to transfer */
    SIZE_T  Size;

    /* [out] Actual number of bytes transferred */
    SIZE_T  BytesTransferred;
} MEM_RW_PARAMS, *PMEM_RW_PARAMS;

#endif // MEMRW_IOCTL_H
```

