## 9. Dockerfile (multi‑stage, minimal)

```dockerfile
# ---------- Build stage ----------
FROM golang:1.22-alpine AS builder

# Install git (needed for go modules) and ca-certificates
RUN apk add --no-cache git ca-certificates

WORKDIR /app

# Cache dependencies
COPY go.mod go.sum ./
RUN go mod download

# Copy source
COPY . .

# Build static binary (disable CGO for fully static image)
ENV CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64
RUN go build -ldflags="-s -w" -o /microservice ./cmd/server

# ---------- Runtime stage ----------
FROM alpine:3.20

# Add a non‑root user
RUN addgroup -S appgroup && adduser -S appuser -G appgroup

# Copy binary from builder
COPY --from=builder /microservice /microservice

# Optional: copy a default .env (or rely on k8s secrets / env vars)
# COPY configs/.env.example ./.env

USER appuser:appgroup

EXPOSE 8080

ENTRYPOINT ["/microservice"]
```

*Build:* `docker build -t microservice:latest .`  
*Run:* `docker run -p 8080:8080 --env-file .env microservice:latest`

