## 13. Checklist for Production Readiness

| ✅ Item | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| **Clean Architecture** | Domain → Use‑case → Infra (DB, Redis, Kafka) → Transport (HTTP). No framework leaks into domain. |
| **Dependency Injection** | All concrete implementations are injected via constructors (`NewOrderService`, `NewPostgresOrderRepo`, …). |
| **Configuration** | Centralised `infra.Load()` with sane defaults, overridable via env or `.env`. |
| **Connection Pooling** | `pgx` pool (`SetMaxOpenConns`, `SetMaxIdleConns`, `SetConnMaxLifetime`). Redis client uses built‑in pooling. |
| **Cache‑Aside** | `GetOrder` tries Redis first, falls back to DB, then writes‑through. |
| **Event Publishing** | Kafka producer wrapped in interface; fire‑and‑forget with error logging (could be made reliable with retries/idempotence). |
| **Observability** | Prometheus counters/histograms for HTTP, DB, cache, Kafka; middleware automatically instruments HTTP. Structured `zap` logging. |
| **Graceful Shutdown** | SIGINT/SIGTRIG triggers HTTP server shutdown, then closes DB, Redis, Kafka. |
| **Timeouts & Context Propagation** | Every external call receives the incoming request context (or a derived timeout). |
| **Error Handling** | Use‑case returns wrapped errors; HTTP layer maps known errors to appropriate status codes; internal errors return 500 without leaking details. |
| **Security** | No SQL injection (pgx uses prepared statements), input validation via `go-playground/validator`, HTTP server sets timeouts, runs as non‑root user in Docker. |
| **CI/CD Friendly** | Single static binary, multi‑stage Dockerfile, `go.mod` versioned, no external scripts needed at runtime. |
| **Testability** | All dependencies are interfaces → easy to mock; example unit test provided. |
| **Documentation** | Inline godoc on handlers (usable with `swag`/`go-swagger`), clear README (this file). |

